    "body": "> Are these steps not necessary as NavigationInterceptHandler is ` Promise<undefined> ()`?\r\n\r\nThat is correct. It is impossible for invoking a promise-returning callback to throw, as any exceptions are converted into rejected promises. See https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invoke-a-callback-function step 11-14, which never allow an exception (abrupt completion) to escape.",
